Third-party software in this sample

The programs in `server/` (the game server, the page server, and the bot) are built with the Go modules
below. The game server uses the Amazon GameLift Servers server SDK and the modules it depends on, and uses
github.com/gorilla/websocket and golang.org/x/net (netutil) directly; the bot uses gorilla/websocket. Each module keeps its own license; the full
license text is in the module's repository and in the module cache after `go mod download`.

| Module | Version | License | Source |
|---|---|---|---|
| github.com/amazon-gamelift/amazon-gamelift-servers-go-server-sdk/v5 | v5.6.0 | Apache-2.0 | https://github.com/amazon-gamelift/amazon-gamelift-servers-go-server-sdk |
| github.com/DataDog/datadog-go/v5 | v5.6.0 | MIT | https://github.com/DataDog/datadog-go |
| github.com/Microsoft/go-winio | v0.5.0 | MIT | https://github.com/microsoft/go-winio |
| github.com/golang/mock | v1.6.0 | Apache-2.0 | https://github.com/golang/mock |
| github.com/google/uuid | v1.5.0 | BSD-3-Clause | https://github.com/google/uuid |
| github.com/gorilla/websocket | v1.5.1 | BSD-3-Clause | https://github.com/gorilla/websocket |
| github.com/sethvargo/go-retry | v0.2.4 | Apache-2.0 | https://github.com/sethvargo/go-retry |
| golang.org/x/net | v0.55.0 | BSD-3-Clause | https://github.com/golang/net |

github.com/Microsoft/go-winio is compiled in only when you build for Windows.

This list covers the modules compiled into the programs under `server/cmd/`. Update it when `server/go.mod` changes.

The AWS Lambda function in `lambda/` uses the AWS SDK for JavaScript that the Lambda Node.js runtime provides;
the sample doesn't bundle it.
